  "minutes": 85,
  "scenario": "Tervani Charpy Lab has 80 invented records: 40 sample/heat pairs, each with LPA and TWA orientations. Sample_no repeats across four heats, so both keys are essential; orientation case/spaces vary and one TWA energy is blank. Missing energy must be reported as Missing, never zero.",
  "lesson": {
    "intro": "Reshaping requires a composite identity. Extract the sample/heat columns and use UNIQUE on whole row pairs. Bring each orientation’s result alongside that same pair, normalizing orientation labels first.",
    "functions": [
      {
        "name": "CHOOSECOLS",
        "purpose": "Select and reorder array columns.",
        "syntax": "=CHOOSECOLS(array, col_num1, [col_num2], ...)",
        "arguments": "Provide an array and 1-based column indices; negative indices count from its right edge.",
        "example": "=CHOOSECOLS({1,2,3;4,5,6},3,1)",
        "result": "3,1 then 6,4",
        "useCase": "Build a compact quality report.",
        "mistake": "Index zero or outside the width errors."
      },
      {
        "name": "CHOOSEROWS",
        "purpose": "Select and reorder array rows.",
        "syntax": "=CHOOSEROWS(array, row_num1, [row_num2], ...)",
        "arguments": "Provide the array and 1-based row indices; negative indices count back from its last row.",
        "example": "=CHOOSEROWS({10;20;30},1,-1)",
        "result": "10 then 30",
        "useCase": "Inspect the first and last records.",
        "mistake": "Indices apply to the current array, after any filtering or sorting."
      },
      {
        "name": "HSTACK",
        "purpose": "Append arrays horizontally.",
        "syntax": "=HSTACK(array1, [array2], ...)",
        "arguments": "Supply arrays to append side by side, with matching row counts.",
        "example": "=HSTACK({1;2},{3;4})",
        "result": "1,3 then 2,4",
        "useCase": "Put orientation results beside sample keys.",
        "mistake": "Different heights cause #N/A padding; row identity must also agree."
      }
    ],
    "combine": "Reuse XLOOKUP from Level 3, TRIM/UPPER from Level 4, and IF for missing energies. Use the two-column key register created by Task 1 as a helper spill. HSTACK preserves alignment only when both returned orientation columns use exactly those keys."
  },
